//
// MEMBERS OF THIS ROW (legal programs the committed compiler still refuses, each
// with a rustc twin that compiles and RUNS at the stated exit code):
//   n05 static-call path exit 3 · n07 three regions transitively exit 7
//   n08 covariant struct Co<'b> exit 3 · n09 Option<&'b i64> parameter exit 4
//   (src/compiler/probes/2026-09-16g-portsarm/battery/, twins in rust/)
// AND ONE HOLE THE ARM ITSELF WOULD OPEN, measured and not rowed because on the
// committed binary the program is correctly REFUSED: `Cell<&'a i64>` carries the
// region in a TYPE ARG, and UnsafeCell's invariance is a LANG-ITEM AXIOM
// (sema_auto_trait.cpp) that the arm's structural pin test cannot see —
// `Cell<T>{inner:UnsafeCell<T>}` over `UnsafeCell<T>{value:T}` bottoms out at a
// bare covariant T. Any future arm must close that too; battery/A_cell.logos.
